      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Both approaches have merit, but the most effective curriculum likely **blends** both to provide a complete picture of the past.\n\nWhile focusing on triumph and shared values can build strong community and a sense of national identity, prioritizing systemic injustice is crucial for developing sophisticated critical thinking and understanding the world's complex power dynamics.\n\nA well-balanced approach allows students to see the context of \"triumphs\" in relation to the \"injustices,\" leading to a more nuanced and powerful understanding of history.",
